// the host (Tomas is the question master: earnest, a little nervous, delighted when you get it right)
// quiz.open: optional, as the card opens. quiz.right: a right answer. quiz.wrong: a wrong one ({answer} = the right
// answer; never a fail). quiz.done: after the third ({n} = right answers, 0-3; reads right for any score).
// quiz.done.perfect / quiz.done.zero: optional, for 3 and 0.
== quiz.open
- Right. Um. Three questions about the Wren. No looking at your device.
- Quiz time! I wrote these myself. Be kind.   #funny
- Three questions. I think they're easy. I think.
== quiz.right
- Correct! A point to the new hand.
- Yes! That's it. I'm so pleased.
- Right! Somebody's been paying attention.
- Spot on. I had to look that one up.   #funny
== quiz.wrong
- Close. It's {answer}.
- Not quite. It's {answer}. Good guess, though.
- Ooh, no. {answer}. I'd have said the same, honestly.
- It's {answer}. Next one's yours.
== quiz.done
- {n} out of 3. Thanks for playing. Same time next week?
- That's {n} out of 3. I'll write harder ones. Or easier. Sort of.   #funny
- {n} out of 3! You came, that's the main thing.   #warm
== quiz.done.perfect
- Three out of three! Have you been reading the walls?   #funny
- A perfect round. I'm genuinely impressed.
== quiz.done.zero
- None this time. Still, you came. That's the best part.   #warm
